--- !u!114 &-9148312288275841351
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 456c7c2b477e4253b9e4faf9ed4b18a9, type: 3}
  m_Name: InstructionsParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.InstructionsParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Title:
    m_Untranslated: Instructions
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "<b>1.</b>  If you are still inside the grill, zoom out and then
      rotate your view (right-click and drag) to face the play structure with a slide.\n\n<b>2.</b> 
      With the <b>Move</b> tool still selected, click directly on the play structure
      in the <b>Scene</b> view to select it, then press <b>F</b> to frame it in view.
      \n\n<b>3.</b> Once the play structure is framed, hold <b>Alt</b> (macOS: <b>Option</b>),
      then <b>left-click</b> and drag with your mouse to orbit around the play structure.
      \n\nYou will find the third hidden number on the bottom of the play structure.\n\n<b>4.</b>
      After you've noted the number, orbit back up around to get a front-facing view
      of the play structure again.\n\nSoon, you'll get so much practice framing and
      orbiting, it will eventually be muscle memory. You also have that shortcut
      cheat sheet to help you remember all the ways you can navigate!"
  m_CriteriaCompletion: 0
  m_Criteria:
    m_Items: []
